0..75 Comment "//! `map`\'s functoriality stated as a law beside the definition it governs:"
76..116 Comment "//! mapping a composite is mapping twice"
117..196 Comment "//! [Bird-1987-an_introduction_to_the_theory_of_lists], § 2. The list `map` of"
197..277 Comment "//! `recursive-lists.gandr` takes its function as a value, and a rule names only"
278..353 Comment "//! its block\'s operations, so the law is stated over `map` presented as an"
354..402 Comment "//! operation with its function defunctionalised"
403..483 Comment "//! [Reynolds-1972-definitional_interpreters_higherorder_programming_languages]:"
484..562 Comment "//! a function is a name `app` applies, and `compose` builds one from two. The"
563..643 Comment "//! coincidence check certifies the law with the definition\'s own rules, and the"
644..724 Comment "//! `normalizes` row fires it. The same law written over the `def` is refused in"
725..778 Comment "//! `../../pathological/data/map-law-on-a-def.gandr`."
779..782 Comment "//!"
783..846 Comment "//! - cites: [Bird-1987-an_introduction_to_the_theory_of_lists]"
847..935 Comment "//! - cites: [Reynolds-1972-definitional_interpreters_higherorder_programming_languages]"
936..939 Comment "//!"
940..1086 Comment "//! [Bird-1987-an_introduction_to_the_theory_of_lists]: https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-87374-4_1 \"Bird, An Introduction to the Theory of Lists\""
1087..1282 Comment "//! [Reynolds-1972-definitional_interpreters_higherorder_programming_languages]: https://doi.org/10.1145/800194.805852 \"Reynolds, Definitional Interpreters for Higher-Order Programming Languages\""
1284..1355 Comment "/// Lists with `map` as an operation: `mapNil` and `mapCons` define it,"
1356..1431 Comment "/// `appCompose` reads a composite, `composeAssoc` orients composition, and"
1432..1495 Comment "/// `mapMap` is the law, mapping twice fused into mapping once."
1496..1498 Other "@["
1499..1509 Other "normalizes"
1509..1510 Other "("
1510..1511 StringLit "\""
1511..1583 StringLit "map(inc, map(dbl, cons(one, nil))) ~> cons(app(inc, app(dbl, one)), nil)"
1583..1584 StringLit "\""
1584..1585 Other ")"
1586..1587 Other "]"
